{"id": "sevt_01XGay98N5Hi7fWzZ53FQN7D", "processed_at": "2026-10-14T11:50:13.517909Z", "tool_use_id": "sevt_014BLfbE5F7STBStHrYwWpHi", "type": "agent.tool_result", "content": [{"text": "1\t---\n2\tname: incident-triage-runbook\n3\tdescription: The SRE team's runbook for triaging production latency and error-rate incidents. Use this whenever investigating an incident, a latency spike, elevated error rates, or when asked \"what caused X\" about a production service.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# Incident triage\n7\t\n8\tIf you change the order below, say why in #sre.\n9\t\n10\t## Order of operations\n11\t\n12\t1. Pull deploys for the last 6h. Don't open the log first.\n13\t2. Line the deploy timestamps up against `p99_latency_ms` / `error_rate` for the paged service. State the gap (\"deploy 14:31, p99 moves 14:33\").\n14\t3. If a deploy lines up: pull the diff, read it. Check for the stuff in the next section.\n15\t4. Then grep the log to confirm. Don't grep to fish.\n16\t5. No deploy lines up \u2192 check `db_pool_utilization` across checkout/cart/auth/inventory, then upstream deps.\n17\t\n18\t## Things that have burned us\n19\t\n20\tIn rough order of how often:\n21\t\n22\t- per-row query where there used to be a batch\n23\t- cache decorator removed \"temporarily\"\n24\t- new query, no index\n25\t- blocking call in an async handler\n26\t- retry loop with no backoff\n27\t\n28\t## Write-up\n29\t\n30\tOne line at the bottom:\n31\t\n32\t> **Root cause:** `<sha>` \u2014 one sentence on the mechanism.\n33\t\n34\tIf it wasn't a deploy, put the component or upstream dep where the sha goes (`db-primary`, `stripe-api`, whatever). Still one sentence.\n35\t\n36\tEverything above that line is evidence. Keep it short; the long version goes in the postmortem doc.\n", "type": "text"}], "is_error": false}
